	Ø Command Prompt 
	- A command prompt, also referred to simple as a prompt, is a short text at the start of the command line followed by prompt symbol on a command line interface
		○ [root@myvm ~]# 
		○ username@hostname~promptsymbol
		○ # for root $ for normal user, it can be modified
	Ø Root
	- There are 3 types of root on Linux system
		○ Root account : root account on linux machine is the most powerful which has access to all commands and files.
		○ Root as / : the very first directory is also referred as root directory
		○ Root home directory : the root user account also has a directory located in /root which is called root home directory 
	
	
